y day i like to end each  day with my character in bed and just  looking at my apartment window and  admiring the dust storms that roll  through i truly believe this is the best  way to play cyberpunk to experience how  much love and detail went into the  environmental storytelling the lighting  and general graphics also just look  amazing on pc romances have been  expanded so you can go have a wholesome  cuddle with pan am or maybe get some  saucy texts this is your chance to go  find adam smasher's secret hideout climb  up to the secret mansion and find out  it's locked now for some reason and  generally just exist in the world stop  and smell the chrome roses take a selfie  with bibi from death stranding ride a  roller coaster with johnny and as the  community put it best for those at end  game meet hanukko at embers nah i don't  think i will  red dead redemption 2 made this list  thanks to a really well made first  person mode the online component may be  dead with the community basically  holding a funeral recently but if you  haven't tried the main story in first  person it winds up being a slow-moving  immersive sim with moments of existence  punctuated by exciting gunfights red  dead 2 is set in an absolutely gorgeous  world particularly on pc and full of  incredible details and stories from  1899. those details are not lost on  weapon models which you can see while  aiming down sights going first person  also lets you get away from rockstar's  usual tiny aiming dot i mean you still  have to turn it off in a menu but it was  always just there designed for a third  person lock-on system you can admire  weapons by inspecting and cleaning them  as well as modify them in shops  first-person melee combat is pretty  brutal in ways you'd miss in third  person on top of guns you also have a  host of gadgets the best being the lasso  which you can use in both gunfights and  when throwing hands it just does not get  old roping somebody in the middle of a  gunfight for people who gravitate  towards more modern weapons there are  few semi-auto pistols later in the game  it's important to remember that red dead  2 does have a classic gta style police  system so if you're on team do crime  you'll become wanted and the law will  chase you through the entire game  finally keep in mind you'll need to  tweak some settings for the best  experience so go in there and change how  the lock on system works set controls to  standard fps and mess with head bobbing  to keep the screen from shaking too much  after that getting to first person view  as a button press and toggling your  weapon to aim down sights is another  button press the game will then remember  everything and you're good to go what  game should be on our next best open  world shooters list our office had  pretty mixed feelings about halo  infinite so tell us why or why not we  should include it on the next one thanks  for watching  oh
 

